<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song.</title><sup><b>1</b></sup> God be merciful unto us, and bless us; <i>and</i> cause his face to shine upon us; Selah.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song.</title><sup><b>2</b></sup> That thy way may be known upon earth, thy saving health among all nations.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song.</title><sup><b>3</b></sup> Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song.</title><sup><b>4</b></sup> O let the nations be glad and sing for joy: for thou shalt judge the people righteously, and govern the nations upon earth. Selah.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song.</title><sup><b>5</b></sup> Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song.</title><sup><b>6</b></sup> <i>Then</i> shall the earth yield her increase; <i>and</i> God, <i>even</i> our own God, shall bless us.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm <i>or</i> Song.</title><sup><b>7</b></sup> God shall bless us; and all the ends of the earth shall fear him. <br />
